---
/**
 * Linked from the footer. Deliberately short: the site collects almost
 * nothing, and saying so plainly is the whole document.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/privacy';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Sonora"
  description="What this site collects, which is almost nothing, and what happens to it."
  path={path}
  schema={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path }])]}
>
  <section class="section privacy">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          This site collects almost nothing. Here is the whole of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Page views are counted with Google Analytics. It sets cookies in your
          browser and records the pages you visit, roughly where in the world you
          are, and what kind of device you used. Google processes that data on
          this site&rsquo;s behalf and may use it for its own purposes under its
          own terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Three things beyond the page views are counted, none of them about
          you: which of the four quiz recommendations came up, that a
          &ldquo;book a call&rdquo; link was clicked and which part of the page
          it was clicked from, and that a form was sent and which form it was.
          Never what you typed into it.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no advertising pixel here and nothing is sold to anyone. Most
          browsers will block these cookies if you ask them to, and the site
          works exactly the same either way. The only other third party involved
          is the web font service that serves the typefaces.
        </p>

        <h2>Forms</h2>
        <p>
          If you submit the contact form or the newsletter form, the details you
          enter are stored by the site host so they can be read and replied to.
          They are not sold, shared, or added to any list other than the one you
          asked to join. The newsletter has an unsubscribe link in every send.
        </p>

        <h2>The &ldquo;find your fit&rdquo; quiz</h2>
        <p>
          The three answers you pick on the services page stay in your browser.
          They are not stored and they are not sent anywhere. The one thing
          recorded is which of the four recommendations came up, counted in
          Google Analytics alongside the page views and the other two events
          above &mdash; so it is possible to see which service people are
          pointed to, and nothing about who was pointed there.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The only cookies this site sets are the Google Analytics ones
          described above. Nothing else on the site stores anything in your
          browser.
        </p>

        <h2>Getting your data removed</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> and say what you would
          like deleted. It gets deleted.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }

  .privacy .lead {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
  }
</style>
